From aadb5f5095dede47424981f1bba18b87e7ed9e55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:17:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 113/113] consensus: set H4T, the lattice tripwire outputs and
 the SLH-DSA block key of the Ark-0 signet

The M4-T and M4-B series leave their Ark-0 values unset: without them
the lattice tripwire rules of leaf version 0xe2 and the
SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s block signature never apply there. Both rules have one
height on Ark-0, H4T, and the three lattice tripwire outputs now exist
on that chain, so this commit fixes all of it, the way patch 65 fixed
the tripwire outputs of leaf version 0xe0.

- ARK0_H4T is 55000, at least 6720 blocks (seven days) after the release
  and late enough for the operator to upgrade its nodes and its
  producer, which carries the SLH output from 1,920 blocks before it.
  ARK0_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE_HEIGHT and ARK0_SLH_BLOCK_HEIGHT both take it
  from that one constant, and a static_assert keeps them equal: from
  that block on every Ark-0 block carries the SLH output, and the same
  block is the first in which leaf version 0xe2 executes.
- ARK0_LATTICE_TRIPWIRES holds the three outputs, all created by
  aac5a1fef01545c338de92bceda520684a49682f2ec546900a4dbe99eba8827c in the
  block at height 39971 (ARK0_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE_CREATION_HEIGHT), each
  with the SHA256 of the ML-DSA-44 key its leaf checks and a label:
  vout 0, "NUMS ML-DSA-44", 591dae31...92805 (the NUMS key); vout 1,
  "destroyed key", c7a02f1f...1df44; vout 2, "drill key",
  5237bdf6...8b495. The third label was "drill" in the constraint the
  outputs are checked against; it is "drill key", as the start-up line
  of the design names it.
- ARK0_SLH_BLOCK_PUBKEY is 012b50fa...41b5e, PK.seed || PK.root, whose
  SHA256 is a64c1077...ef569.

Static asserts hold the values together: the order of the Ark-0 heights,
8600 < 20000 < 30000 < 32000 <= H4T; the creation height below H4T, so
that the outputs count as present when the rules start; three distinct
outpoints of one transaction, the first with the NUMS key; the SLH
height equal to H4T; and, as before, the SLH key set exactly when its
height is finite. Changing H4T later is the constant, its tests and its
docs.

With the values set, the paths the two series already had for a decided
Ark-0 apply: the consensus parameters carry the height, the outputs with
their labels and key hashes, and signet_slh_block; an Ark-0 node logs
"Signet P2MR lattice tripwire rules from height 55000 in leaf version
0xe2; tripwire outputs ..." with the three outpoints, labels and key
hashes, and "Signet SLH-DSA block signature required from height 55000,
public key SHA256 ..."; OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S logs leaf version 0xe2 among
its leaf versions; getdeploymentinfo lists p2mr_lattice_tripwire at
55000; gettripwireinfo reports the three outputs. The line that said the
lattice tripwire rules are not active on Ark-0 is gone, with the include
it needed. Both options stay refused on Ark-0.

The ark0_inactive unit tests become ark0: the deployment height, the
outpoints, labels and key hashes, the creation cutoff (an output created
at 39971 is present, one created at or above H4T is not), the script
flags and the ML-DSA-44 state around the height, and the SLH height and
key, with a block without the SLH output passing below H4T and refused
from it. The functional tests check the Ark-0 node's lines, RPCs and the
refused options. feature_signet_slhblock_lattice.py turns the ad hoc
check of the join of M4-T and M4-B into a test: one custom signet with
both rules from one height, blocks signed SLH first, then ML-DSA-44,
below, at and above it, a block without the SLH output refused as
bad-signet-slhblk with the lattice state unchanged, the four start-up
lines and the separate dependency checks; and a second one shaped like
Ark-0, with the three outputs created below the height, where an
ML-DSA-44 spend of leaf version 0xe2 is accepted below the height and
after it while the outputs are present, and refused once the drill
output is spent, while an SLH-DSA spend of 0xe2 is still accepted.
