+### Lattice tripwire outputs
+
+On Ark-0 the three outputs are P2MR outputs of two leaves of version `0xc0` at depth one: the
+ML-DSA-44 template S1 of a key, and `OP_RETURN`, 10,000 sats each, all created by transaction
+`aac5a1fef01545c338de92bceda520684a49682f2ec546900a4dbe99eba8827c` in the block at height 39971
+(`ARK0_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE_CREATION_HEIGHT`). The leaf with the key cannot be of version `0xe2`:
 before the height anyone could spend it, and after a trigger it could not be spent at all.
 `OP_CHECKMLDSA44` in `0xc0` is never disabled.
 
-| Output | Key | Label |
-|---|---|---|
-| L1 | the NUMS key below: nobody has a secret for it | `NUMS ML-DSA-44` |
-| L2 | generated once, its secret destroyed (the operator says so; it cannot be proved) | `destroyed key` |
-| L3 | the operator holds it and spends it at an announced time to trigger the drill | `drill` |
+| Output | Outpoint | Key | Label | SHA-256 of the public key |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| L1 | `aac5a1fe…eba8827c:0` | the NUMS key below: nobody has a secret for it | `NUMS ML-DSA-44` | `591dae318a0fdde81a590eab8c8581e07657d2c30b97cf31d87bafe636c92805` |
+| L2 | `aac5a1fe…eba8827c:1` | generated once, its secret destroyed (the operator says so; it cannot be proved) | `destroyed key` | `c7a02f1f92cb9b73dc324dab81e85737b43cbc06acf8c3d959e68153eaa1df44` |
+| L3 | `aac5a1fe…eba8827c:2` | the operator holds it and spends it at an announced time to trigger the drill | `drill key` | `5237bdf62ebe594076000f2231b7fcf741e01a7482ffa64f50cc3ce14c28b495` |
