+## Ark-0
+
+On the Ark-0 signet the rule is fixed in the code, with no option to change it:
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Height | 55000 (`ARK0_SLH_BLOCK_HEIGHT`, equal to `ARK0_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE_HEIGHT`: one constant, `ARK0_H4T`, holds both) |
+| Public key (`PK.seed \|\| PK.root`) | `012b50fafe6e265ce48cb16b0c28cfe25957c6b9410e353bcb88733b9a841b5e` |
+| SHA-256 of the public key | `a64c10772542226abe2b1495b2576f50773d3725c5065f48abb5d4559fdef569` |
+
+An Ark-0 node logs
+
+    Signet SLH-DSA block signature required from height 55000, public key SHA256 a64c10772542226abe2b1495b2576f50773d3725c5065f48abb5d4559fdef569
+
+The ML-DSA-44 block signature it relies on is required there from height 20000.
+From height 55000 every Ark-0 block carries the SLH output, and the first block
+at that height is also the first in which leaf version `0xe2` executes; the two
+rules share no state, and each checks the block as on its own
+(`feature_signet_slhblock_lattice.py` runs both from one height on a custom
+signet). The producer must start putting the SLH output in its blocks at least
+1,920 blocks (about 48 hours at its fastest rate) before the height, so that a
+wrong signature shows in the nodes' logs (`-debug=validation`) well before it
+would stop the chain. Once a build carrying the height and the key has been
+published, neither changes.
+
